{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1477, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nOn the two-dimensional coordinate plane, there is an infinite tiling of 1 \\times 1 squares.\nConsider drawing a circle of radius R centered at the center of one of these squares. How many of these squares are completely contained inside the circle?\nMore precisely, find the number of integer pairs (i,j) such that all four points (i+0.5,j+0.5), (i+0.5,j-0.5), (i-0.5,j+0.5), and (i-0.5,j-0.5) are at a distance of at most R from the origin.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nR\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq R \\leq 10^{6}\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n2\n\nSample Output 1\n\n5\r\n\nThere are a total of five squares completely contained in the circle: the square whose center matches the circle\u2019s center, plus the four squares adjacent to it.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4\n\nSample Output 2\n\n37\n\nSample Input 3\n\n26\n\nSample Output 3\n\n2025\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1507, "char_start": 1489, "quote": "Input:\n2\nOutput:\n5", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1538, "char_start": 1519, "quote": "Input:\n4\nOutput:\n37", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1572, "char_start": 1550, "quote": "Input:\n26\nOutput:\n2025", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "059ed2a85a54f68e1d10801a6d1c2646cd52b3a3bdfb999af552a4209294415e", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "94755e053a693f4f933315d3ac5038f35e6b877d7001fefd9c5fa02f3e3fec2f", "seq": 2}
